WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.863
Collection should minimize unnecessary changes while preserving enough evidence to answer the investigation questions.

00:00:06.863 --> 00:00:15.498
macOS systems may use FileVault encryption, Apple Silicon security controls, user privacy protections, endpoint management, and cloud synchronization.

00:00:15.498 --> 00:00:21.919
Those features can affect what is available and how collection should be performed.

00:00:21.919 --> 00:00:27.897
The collection plan should be authorized, documented, and matched to the case.

00:00:27.897 --> 00:00:40.516
Disk images, snapshots, targeted collections, memory capture at a high level, log exports, user profile artifacts, plists, application data, and endpoint security exports can all be useful.

00:00:40.516 --> 00:00:50.922
The right approach depends on urgency, system availability, data sensitivity, legal requirements, and whether the device is live, locked, remote, or managed.

00:00:50.922 --> 00:00:56.900
Reports should explain the collection method because it affects confidence and limitations.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.107
Hashes help verify whether evidence changes after collection.

00:01:01.107 --> 00:01:11.955
Chain of custody records document what was collected, where it came from, who handled it, when it moved, and how it was stored.

00:01:11.955 --> 00:01:17.933
Case notes should record commands, tools, timestamps, observations, decisions, assumptions, and limitations.

00:01:17.933 --> 00:01:23.468
These records help future reviewers separate investigator activity from system activity.

00:01:23.468 --> 00:01:29.003
Reporting should include methods, evidence, findings, confidence, limitations, and supporting references.

00:01:29.003 --> 00:01:35.424
macOS artifacts can be complex, application-specific, and affected by privacy settings or synchronization.

00:01:35.424 --> 00:01:38.745
A good report avoids unsupported certainty.

00:01:38.745 --> 00:01:46.494
It explains what the evidence supports, what remains unknown, and what additional sources might improve confidence.
